cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the Implementation Guide, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Shoulder on FHIR — a FHIR R4 Implementation Guide for standardized rotator cuff surgery documentation"
abstract: >-
  A FHIR R4 Implementation Guide and demonstration system for standardized
  documentation of rotator cuff injuries and their surgical treatment in
  research registries, developed as a master's thesis at the Hasso Plattner
  Institute. Bundles the FSH source and generated conformance resources, two
  demonstration frontends (a typed-builder application and an HL7 SDC-driven
  questionnaire application), the SECEC->FHIR element-coverage mapping, and two
  longitudinal example-patient walkthroughs.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Maximilian
    family-names: Purk
    affiliation: "Hasso Plattner Institute, University of Potsdam"
repository-code: "https://github.com/maxpurk/shoulder-on-fhir"
license:
  - Apache-2.0   # code: frontends, scripts, deployment configuration, tooling
  - CC-BY-4.0    # Implementation Guide content: FSH source, narrative, conformance resources
keywords:
  - FHIR
  - HL7
  - Implementation Guide
  - rotator cuff
  - orthopaedics
  - shoulder surgery
  - clinical registry
  - interoperability
# The version and release date are filled in and uncommented when a tagged
# release of this Implementation Guide is published. There is no DOI field:
# the tagged release in this repository is the fixed reference point, and it
# is reachable only while the repository itself is reachable.
version: "1.0.0-thesis"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
